        "## Part 1: Tuples\n",
        "### Locking In the Crew\n",
        "\n",
        "Every person on this crew has a role, and those roles do not change once the job starts. Swapping responsibilities mid-operation gets people caught.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is where **tuples** come in.\n",
        "\n",
        "A tuple is a collection of data, just like a list. The difference is that a tuple is **immutable**, which means you cannot change it after it is created. You access items in a tuple the same way you do a list, using an index.\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "my_tuple = (\"item one\", \"item two\", \"item three\")\n",
        "print(my_tuple[0])  # prints: item one\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "The crew's information is stored in tuples using this format:\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "(name, role, years_of_experience)\n",
        "```"
      ]
    },
