        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Part 3: Sets\n",
        "### Tracking the Scouted Areas\n",
        "\n",
        "Dex has been driving past the estate every day this week, logging which areas the crew has already scoped out. A location should never appear twice on the list. Marking the same spot twice wastes time and risks drawing attention.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is where sets come in. A set is a collection that **does not allow duplicates**. If you try to add something that is already in the set, nothing happens. It just stays the same.\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "my_set = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n",
        "my_set.add(\"apple\")  # already there, nothing changes\n",
        "print(my_set)        # {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Note: Sets do not have a guaranteed order, so do not be surprised if the items print in a different order each time."
      ]
    },
